{# Listed weeks per calendar month for one water. Needs: water, water_months
   (None below three listed weeks, which shows nothing). Counts come from the
   weeks CDFW listed for this water since the record began; removed entries
   are not counted, and a month that is not shown has no listed week. #}
{% if water_months %}
<section class="water-months" aria-labelledby="water-months-heading">
  <h2 id="water-months-heading">{{ water.name }} by month in the weeks recorded here</h2>
  <p>
    In the weeks recorded here, since the {{ water_months.since_label }},
    {{ water.name }} was on CDFW's schedule for {{ water_months.total }}
    {{ "week" if water_months.total == 1 else "weeks" }} across
    {{ water_months.month_count }} {{ "month" if water_months.month_count == 1 else "months" }}.
    {% if water_months.peak_tied %}{{ water_months.peak_months }} share the highest count, {{ water_months.peak_weeks }} {{ "week" if water_months.peak_weeks == 1 else "weeks" }} each.{% else %}{{ water_months.peak_months }} has the highest count, with {{ water_months.peak_weeks }} {{ "week" if water_months.peak_weeks == 1 else "weeks" }}.{% endif %}
  </p>
  <table>
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Weeks {{ water.name }} was on CDFW's schedule, by month, since the {{ water_months.since_label }}</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Weeks on the schedule</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in water_months.rows %}
      <tr><td>{{ row.month }}</td><td>{{ row.weeks }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="muted">
    A week counts in the month it begins. A month missing from the table has no
    listed week in this record; the record does not say what happened in it.
    This is a count of recorded weeks, not a forecast, and a record this short
    is not a full season.
  </p>
</section>
{% endif %}
